# 6. Azure CLI Login and Subscription

After installing Azure CLI, authenticate with Azure.

```bash
az login
```

View the active subscription:

```bash
az account show
```

List available subscriptions:

```bash
az account list
```

Set the required subscription:

```bash
az account set --subscription "<subscription-name-or-id>"
```

Official reference:

[Azure CLI Account Commands](https://learn.microsoft.com/cli/azure/account)

---

# 7. Azure Resource Groups

A Resource Group is a logical container for Azure resources.

[Azure Resource Groups Documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/manage-resource-groups-portal)

Resource Groups help organize resources that belong to the same application,
environment, or lifecycle.

FlavorForge uses:

```text
Resource Group
    flavorforge-rg
        |
        +---- Azure Container Registry
        |
        +---- Azure Kubernetes Service
```

---

# 8. Resource Group — Azure CLI Reference

Azure CLI can be used to create a Resource Group.

Example:

```bash
az group create \
  --name <resource-group-name> \
  --location <azure-region>
```

List Resource Groups:

```bash
az group list --output table
```

Show a Resource Group:

```bash
az group show \
  --name <resource-group-name>
```

Delete a Resource Group:

```bash
az group delete \
  --name <resource-group-name>
```

Official reference:

[Azure CLI Resource Group Commands](https://learn.microsoft.com/cli/azure/group)

> **Important:** Deleting a Resource Group can delete the resources contained
> within it. Use the delete command carefully.

