# 10. Azure Container Registry (ACR)

Azure Container Registry is Microsoft's managed private container registry
service.

[Azure Container Registry Documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/container-registry/)

ACR is used to store and manage Docker and OCI container images.

Conceptually:

```text
Developer / CI Pipeline
          |
          v
     Docker Build
          |
          v
   Container Image
          |
          v
 Azure Container Registry
          |
          v
           AKS
```

FlavorForge uses ACR as the container image registry for its frontend and
backend images.

---

# 11. ACR — Azure CLI Reference

The Azure CLI provides commands for creating and managing ACR.

[Azure CLI ACR Commands](https://learn.microsoft.com/cli/azure/acr)

Example:

```bash
az acr create \
  --resource-group <resource-group-name> \
  --name <registry-name> \
  --sku Basic
```

List registries:

```bash
az acr list --output table
```

Show registry information:

```bash
az acr show \
  --name <registry-name> \
  --resource-group <resource-group-name>
```

---

# 12. ACR Login

Azure CLI can authenticate Docker to an Azure Container Registry.

```bash
az acr login \
  --name <registry-name>
```

This allows Docker commands to interact with the registry.

Official reference:

[az acr login](https://learn.microsoft.com/cli/azure/acr#az-acr-login)

---

# 13. ACR Images and Repositories

ACR stores container repositories and image tags.

List repositories:

```bash
az acr repository list \
  --name <registry-name> \
  --output table
```

List tags:

```bash
az acr repository show-tags \
  --name <registry-name> \
  --repository <repository-name>
```

Official reference:

[Azure Container Registry Repositories](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/container-registry/container-registry-get-started-azure-cli)

FlavorForge uses versioned Docker images that are pushed to ACR and later
referenced by Kubernetes workloads.

---

# 14. ACR Authentication and AKS

AKS needs permission to pull private images from ACR.

Azure provides supported integration between AKS and ACR.

[Authenticate with Azure Container Registry from Azure Kubernetes Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/aks/cluster-container-registry-integration)

Conceptually:

```text
                Azure
                  |
       +----------+----------+
       |                     |
       v                     v
      ACR                    AKS
       |                     |
 Docker Images          Kubernetes Pods
       |                     |
       +------ Pull ---------+
```

This is an important concept when deploying private container images to AKS.

