# 17. Create an AKS Cluster

The Azure CLI can be used to create an AKS cluster.

Example:

```bash
az aks create \
  --resource-group <resource-group-name> \
  --name <aks-cluster-name> \
  --node-count 2 \
  --generate-ssh-keys
```

Official reference:

[Create an AKS Cluster with Azure CLI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/aks/learn/quick-kubernetes-deploy-cli)

FlavorForge uses:

```text
AKS Cluster
flavorforge-aks

Region
East US

Node Count
2

Node Size
Standard_D2as_v7
```

These values are project-specific and should be verified against the actual
Azure environment when reproducing the project.

---

# 18. Connect to AKS

After creating an AKS cluster, retrieve Kubernetes credentials:

```bash
az aks get-credentials \
  --resource-group <resource-group-name> \
  --name <aks-cluster-name>
```

Then verify the connection:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

Official reference:

[Connect to an AKS Cluster](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/aks/learn/quick-kubernetes-deploy-cli)

This creates or updates the local Kubernetes configuration used by `kubectl`.

