# 19. AKS and Kubernetes

AKS provides the managed Azure infrastructure while Kubernetes provides the
container orchestration layer.

```text
Azure
  |
  v
AKS
  |
  v
Kubernetes
  |
  +---- Namespace
  |
  +---- Deployment
  |
  +---- Pods
  |
  +---- Services
  |
  +---- ConfigMaps
  |
  +---- Secrets
  |
  +---- HPA
```

This distinction is important:

> **AKS is Microsoft's managed Kubernetes service. Kubernetes is the
> orchestration platform running within AKS.**

