# 20. AKS Scaling

AKS supports scaling of the Kubernetes cluster and its workloads.

[Scale an AKS Cluster](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/aks/scale-cluster)

There are two different concepts:

### Cluster Scaling

Changes the number or size of Kubernetes nodes.

### Workload Scaling

Changes the number of application Pods.

FlavorForge uses Kubernetes workload mechanisms such as Deployments and HPA.
These should not be confused with scaling the underlying AKS node pool.

