# 34. Recommended Learning Principle

> **Understand the Azure service first, create it using Azure CLI second,
> verify the actual Azure resource third, and connect it to the application
> only after the resource is confirmed.**

For example:

```text
Create Resource Group
        ↓
Verify Resource Group
        ↓
Create ACR
        ↓
Verify ACR
        ↓
Create AKS
        ↓
Verify AKS
        ↓
Connect AKS to ACR
        ↓
Verify Kubernetes access
        ↓
Deploy FlavorForge
```

Useful verification commands include:

```bash
az group show --name <resource-group-name>

az acr show \
  --name <registry-name> \
  --resource-group <resource-group-name>

az aks show \
  --name <aks-cluster-name> \
  --resource-group <resource-group-name>

az aks get-credentials \
  --resource-group <resource-group-name> \
  --name <aks-cluster-name>

kubectl get nodes
```

